Encapsulation is one of the concepts of OOPs. It states that all the data members(variables) and member functions (methods) should be grouped, bind or wrapped into
a single emtity called as Class. The best example of Encapsulation is Java Bean Class. 
A Java Bean Class is the one which has following properties:
i) It should be a public non-abstract(concrete) class.
ii) The variables of the class should be declared as private.
iii) There should be separate setter and getter methods for each data member(variables).

Java Bean Class or Encapsulation is helpful.
i) To validate data before assigning it to the variables (using conditional statements in setter functions).
ii) It improves the code readability.
iii) It protects the data from illogical assignment of data.
iv) It makes the code more flexible and secure, we can make the data either write only(by defining only the setter function), read only(by defining only the getter
functiom) and both by defining both functions.

                                                                                       
The shortcut to create getter and setter methods is Alt + Shift + S.                                                                                                                    
